@* The invisible catcher a dropdown lays over the page so a click anywhere else closes it.
   Rendered only while the menu is open, and only ever beneath it — z-20 against the menu's
   z-30 (see .field-menu).

   The three menus that need one had two copies of it and one omission: the seat picker on the
   setup screen had none at all, so the only way to shut it was to pick something or to open
   another. A button rather than a div, so the catcher is a real control rather than a div with
   a click handler — tabindex="-1" keeps it out of the tab order (there is nothing to do here
   but dismiss, and Escape is the keyboard's way out) and aria-hidden keeps it out of the
   accessibility tree, where a nameless full-page control would be noise.

   Not ModalShell's backdrop: that one dims the page because a dialog takes it over. A dropdown
   does not, so this paints nothing. *@

<button type="button" class="fixed inset-0 z-20 cursor-default" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"
        @onclick="OnDismiss"></button>

@code {
    /// <summary>Raised when the click lands outside — the host closes its own menu.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback OnDismiss { get; set; }
}
